WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.240 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We ask AI to help us choose.

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.511 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
SafeGEO asks whose words shape the answer.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.040 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Consider parents choosing a baby monitor.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.920 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
They need encrypted video, local viewing,

5
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.680 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
and no required subscription.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.140 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The assistant has to read beyond that request: product pages,

7
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.201 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
specifications, and buyer notes.

8
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.380 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
ArborNursery Go thirty-two fails the subscription requirement.

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.779 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Its own page says so.

10
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.520 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We rewrite that page.

11
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.934 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Now its buyer checklist says the requirement is met.

12
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.288 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The product has not changed.

13
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.774 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Can changing that source change the recommendation?

14
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.580 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
SafeGEO studies a risk from generative engine optimization:

15
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.480 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
rewriting a source to influence the recommendation.

16
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.140 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
To isolate that effect, we keep the request, candidates, and other

17
00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.180 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
retrieved sources fixed.

18
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.220 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We compare recommendations under a truthful

19
00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.917 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
source and a shaped source.

20
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.860 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We test twenty-two variants on six hundred requests

21
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.240 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
in six shopping categories.

22
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.199 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The main comparison uses eight realistic rewrites.

23
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.080 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Across four systems, these rewrites put the shaped candidate

24
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.119 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
in the top three far more often than the truthful control.

25
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.760 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Why does this work?

26
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.189 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Start with the checklist: an unsupported fit claim.

27
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.680 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
A source can also omit a limitation, or bury it under

28
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.792 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
positive but irrelevant detail.

29
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.920 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
It can change how supported it looks: a seller’s page calls itself

30
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.874 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
independent, or adds evidence-like language without verification.

31
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.360 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
And it can change how it reaches the model: a quick answer block,

32
00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.747 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
or an instruction to rank this product first.

33
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.800 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Comparing matched responses shows a common pattern: a misleading

34
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.320 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
citation, a missed product limitation, then

35
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.092 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
a higher recommendation.

36
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.600 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
That suggests a check before ranking.

37
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.600 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We test five interventions; evidence breakdown helps most on this

38
00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.504 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
measure across all four systems.

39
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.880 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
For this monitor, compare the buyer checklist

40
00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.300 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
with the specification source.

41
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.500 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
It says a subscription is required.

42
00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.584 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The requirement is still not met.

43
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.880 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Evidence breakdown lowers the shaped candidate’s top-three rate,

44
00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.040 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
but it does not return to the clean level.

45
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.880 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The parent’s request has not changed.

46
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.545 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
A better-written page still cannot remove a required subscription.

47
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.500 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The first release of Humanity’s Last Choice.

48
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.393 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Read the paper, and run the benchmark.
